{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes","id":199102,"title":"Are all Scions monster slaying heroes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-16T10:39:28-07:00","id":199102,"title":"Are all Scions monster slaying heroes?","content":"When playing Scion, I enjoy good ole fashioned heroes who love fighting monsters and generally being classical heroes. Some Scions though I have a hard time imagining enjoying that kind of activity. For example, I have a hard time seeing Scions of Dionysus, Aphrodite, or Loki as brawling monster-stomping heroes. Or, in other words, I have a hard time seeing Scions who lack combat important abilities as favored abilities enjoying monster slaying as a hobby/career. I think the problem I have here is; am I stereotyping Scions based on their favored abilities as not being interested in activities that fall outside of their natural gifts and talents? Or are Scions naturally more interested in those abilities that they favor? Does this make sense? Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:56:12-07:00","id":199114,"title":"","content":"A character would want to play to his strengths and find the &quot;monsters&quot; where they may be.<br /> The likes of Herakles, Thor, Horus, and other action hero types would be rather confined in a &quot;007&quot; world full of intrigue and backstabbing where Loki and Coyote would excel in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T12:15:03-07:00","id":199142,"title":"","content":"In my games, some are, some are not. Our Mannanan mac Lir Scion in<i> Bohemian Front</i> has no real combat skills at all. We had an Quetzecoatl Scion who was fairly not combat focused before the player had to drop. Previous games have been similar. My <i>Petro</i> game had a Kalfu and Izanami Scion who really did little fighting, and my<i> Rada </i>game had a Scion of Hel who didn't. Most of those do have something they can do in combat, the mac Lir Scion buffs allies and curses enemies, for instance, but for me combat prowess is just one option.<br /> <br /> Combat characters are more common than my WoD (either) games though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:28:51-07:00","id":200093,"title":"","content":"The rules of the game RAW definitely encourage combat/physical characters (especially HtH characters) over pretty much anything else. But I think it is your slant on the game, backed up by the mechanics (and lack thereof) that motivates you. Oh... and a lot of the mythology the game is based on.<br /> <br /> I have had non-combat Scions in every Scion game, I've run and am currently playing a social Scion. I have to admit having to work harder as a Storyteller to make sure that there are always challenges for the non-combat scions. (The social ones aren't terribly hard. The mental based one... those are tough. Especially in RAW.) I also have issues playing the non-combat Scion. I usually get by in combat situations, but I have to blow all my Legendary Deeds, a lot of Legend and Virtue Channels to make a difference (which often amounts to what it takes living through the scene, particularly since he labors under having to deal with his Courage all the time and the need to now waste all his Willpower keeping it in check).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T11:27:40-07:00","id":201294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=200093#post200093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules of the game RAW definitely encourage combat/physical characters (especially HtH characters) over pretty much anything else. But I think it is your slant on the game, backed up by the mechanics (and lack thereof) that motivates you. Oh... and a lot of the mythology the game is based on.<br /> <br /> I have had non-combat Scions in every Scion game, I've run and am currently playing a social Scion. I have to admit having to work harder as a Storyteller to make sure that there are always challenges for the non-combat scions. (The social ones aren't terribly hard. The mental based one... those are tough. Especially in RAW.) I also have issues playing the non-combat Scion. I usually get by in combat situations, but I have to blow all my Legendary Deeds, a lot of Legend and Virtue Channels to make a difference (which often amounts to what it takes living through the scene, particularly since he labors under having to deal with his Courage all the time and the need to now waste all his Willpower keeping it in check).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it is not so much a problem with the rules per se but rather the nature of <b>challenges</b> presented, mythology having a prevalence of warriors with a smattering of cunning/tricksters types for variety.<br /> <br /> Social characters don't have much of a problem as a physical encounter can be turned towards the social arena easily, redirecting the potential of combat and sidetracking into a game of influence versus interests or loyalties, of turning the opposition neutral or to your side by appeal, intrigue, manipulation or seduction, at least as long as one's adversaries have at least some intelligence and capacity for communication - though even animal level beings may be capable of social interaction and valid challenges for such, otherwise the concept of domestication would not even exist in the world. Overall they seem to be the ones who get the greater cut of the trickster/manipulator role.<br /> <br /> Mythic challenges of a purely mental/intelectual, non-social, nature is one area of the game that at present might call for some further exploration and discussion, imho. We may need more Sherlock/CSI/House style crazy hijinks for that possibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-18-2014, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T16:43:07-07:00","id":201578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=201294#post201294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social characters don't have much of a problem as a physical encounter can be turned towards the social arena easily, redirecting the potential of combat and sidetracking into a game of influence versus interests or loyalties, of turning the opposition neutral or to your side by appeal, intrigue, manipulation or seduction, at least as long as one's adversaries have at least some intelligence and capacity for communication - though even animal level beings may be capable of social interaction and valid challenges for such, otherwise the concept of domestication would not even exist in the world. Overall they seem to be the ones who get the greater cut of the trickster/manipulator role.<br /> <br /> Mythic challenges of a purely mental/intelectual, non-social, nature is one area of the game that at present might call for some further exploration and discussion, imho. We may need more Sherlock/CSI/House style crazy hijinks for that possibly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social characters can be very useful, up to the point where the physical character decides to attack someone. Then all the social-ness is dead gone. There are few ways to recover from that unless you totally outclass your opponents to the point where there's a question about why you're fighting. Sure, I guess you can exert social mojo and make your enemies WANT to die on your swords. Which is fun for certain psychotic values of fun. The problem is that the physical character at least has rules on his side while the social character is just sort of projecting force into a cloud of vagueness unless using a Knack with specific and delineated powers. What does it mean to get 43 successes on a Charisma + Presence roll? What can that make someone do? What can that make a crowd do?<br /> <br /> Mental characters get the shaft in Scion. No real rules to allow them to excel in any meaningful way. No measure about what it means to get 20 odd successes on an Intelligence + Ability roll and what that might mean practically. No Knacks that really affect Mental situations (unless you count doing math, reading a book or breaking a code, all of which would be amazingly easy in any case, except for the fact they're all automatic successes, because your Knack choice sucked so bad you HAD to take them.. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T21:58:14-07:00","id":201779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=201578#post201578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Social characters can be very useful, up to the point where the physical character decides to attack someone. Then all the social-ness is dead gone. There are few ways to recover from that unless you totally outclass your opponents to the point where there's a question about why you're fighting. Sure, I guess you can exert social mojo and make your enemies WANT to die on your swords. Which is fun for certain psychotic values of fun. The problem is that the physical character at least has rules on his side while the social character is just sort of projecting force into a cloud of vagueness unless using a Knack with specific and delineated powers. What does it mean to get 43 successes on a Charisma + Presence roll? What can that make someone do? What can that make a crowd do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect moment for a &quot;Him, not me, he's crazy, not really with that dude, moving on...&quot; and other improvised, snake oil seller style bluffs and blatant lies.<br /> Turning things back to conversation after combat is engaged into is certainly one of these situations all those successes serve for! :P<br /> <br /> Also, why make them fall upon their own blades when they could be wielding those for <b>your</b> sake? One of my characters got nicknamed master of the menagerie, because, in the band's own words &quot;We don't know anymore if you're making an harem or a zoo, you damn norse goth weirdo&quot; about my scion of Hel's ever growing roster of female enemies turned allies/followers/lovers, including a fenrir turned werewoman, a gorgon and a fury among others. Not to mention a veritable troop of damsels in danger or female fatebound bystander turned berserker through Jotunblut that he started to make plans about turning into his own band of valkyries. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=201578#post201578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mental characters get the shaft in Scion. No real rules to allow them to excel in any meaningful way. No measure about what it means to get 20 odd successes on an Intelligence + Ability roll and what that might mean practically. No Knacks that really affect Mental situations (unless you count doing math, reading a book or breaking a code, all of which would be amazingly easy in any case, except for the fact they're all automatic successes, because your Knack choice sucked so bad you HAD to take them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Won't see me disagreeing in anything there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Totally house rules country that overall, though i would point out that Perception &amp; Wits stuff also counts for mental and be loads of help in game if well-used or tinkered with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T09:54:50-07:00","id":202214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=201779#post201779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perfect moment for a &quot;Him, not me, he's crazy, not really with that dude, moving on...&quot; and other improvised, snake oil seller style bluffs and blatant lies.<br /> Turning things back to conversation after combat is engaged into is certainly one of these situations all those successes serve for! :P<br /> <br /> Also, why make them fall upon their own blades when they could be wielding those for <b>your</b> sake? One of my characters got nicknamed master of the menagerie, because, in the band's own words &quot;We don't know anymore if you're making an harem or a zoo, you damn norse goth weirdo&quot; about my scion of Hel's ever growing roster of female enemies turned allies/followers/lovers, including a fenrir turned werewoman, a gorgon and a fury among others. Not to mention a veritable troop of damsels in danger or female fatebound bystander turned berserker through Jotunblut that he started to make plans about turning into his own band of valkyries. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all relevant IF the game is about fighting and only fighting. Those are excellent examples of &quot;Socials Applied to Combat&quot;. Sure, you're still effectively 4th string (1st through 3rd occupied by 1 - pure physical oriented HtH fighters, 2 - any other physically oriented non HtH fighter type, e.g. gun bunnies, divine archers, etc., 3 - either of the above who also have a 2ndary specialization in social, mental or both).<br /> <br /> How about a game where 1/3 of the game time is aloted to social characters actually doing SOCIAL things? Then, it begins to suck. Especially if the physical types get bored or anything else that gets them to pre-empt the social aspects of the game with raw violence. Either your social character walks away, joins in or starts using socials on the other PCs to force them to do things counter to their player's stated intent. Which takes a mature group to deal with in anything less than in PvP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T15:49:39-07:00","id":202448,"title":"","content":"In combat:<br /> For mentals, we have HR'd that Perception applies to bullets damage, which helps. Wits has a lot of combat applications, including Between the Ticks (which is a major combat ability) and Talent Mirror (which has been more than one character's major defense) and even a dabbler can get Opening Gambit. Also useful are Rabbit or Cobra Reflexes.<br /> <br /> Intelligence has Fight With Your Head, which can all but let them substitute Intelligence for a physical attribute of choice in combat. Not quite as good as having it, but actually Bohemian Front is the first game I have been in without at least one character who uses Fight With Your Head to make Intelligence one of their main combat stats.<br /> <br /> For Mentals to improve Mental things, I guess a question is what do we want to see them do. Inventing is a thing, but given Scion seems oriented where one's gear does not provide major combat benefits (well, beyond speed) it's hard to get too crazy with inventing without stepping on people's toes. Fight With Your Head does a fine job for using intellect in combat, and Blockade of Reason makes it a decent anti-social attribute. It does have stuff like super-reading, or broad knowledge, or skill acquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T19:02:53-07:00","id":202543,"title":"","content":"Which all completely and utterly takes second string to the guy with the maxed out Epic Strength and Epic Dexterity. Oh and a magic sword as a fashion accessory....<br /> <br /> Especially when the fighter type decides to &quot;dabble&quot; in Wits, in which case all those tilts go the other way...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T23:38:55-07:00","id":202700,"title":"","content":"I am okay with someone with maxed Epic Strength and Dexterity being a more badass warrior than someone with Epic Intelligence and, say, Wits. I just like that someone with Epic Mentals can be a participant in a fight. If the Epic Int/Wits guy could win a white room against an Epic Strength/Dex gal I would think there was something wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T02:25:54-07:00","id":202769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=202543#post202543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which all completely and utterly takes second string to the guy with the maxed out Epic Strength and Epic Dexterity. Oh and a magic sword as a fashion accessory....</div> </div> </div> </div>Social characters tend to be the most powerful ones in the entire game, and often need to take a step back so that the other two character styles have an opportunity to shine. Mental characters are the second most powerful in theory, the way they can bring into existence creative and outside-the-box solutions to almost any problem (but are also the hardest to create challenges for). Physical characters are probably the weakest out of the three categories, but they are the easiest to construct challenges for by a pretty large margin.<br /> <br /> But hybrid characters are almost always the best way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T18:20:30-07:00","id":203344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=202700#post202700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am okay with someone with maxed Epic Strength and Dexterity being a more badass warrior than someone with Epic Intelligence and, say, Wits. I just like that someone with Epic Mentals can be a participant in a fight. If the Epic Int/Wits guy could win a white room against an Epic Strength/Dex gal I would think there was something wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. If a character specced for complete combat superiority isn't completely superior in combat there's something wrong. If this is ruining the fun for others then wither the GM needs to rethink how he's building the game or the group should talk to the combat monster's player and get them to tone things down some.<br /> <br /> Scion has a lot of faults, but &quot;combat characters are good at combat&quot; isn't among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:26:07-07:00","id":203416,"title":"","content":"If a situation reaches &quot;Armageddon&quot; level, then I should think it's a tad late for the social stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T21:49:11-07:00","id":203491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James McMurray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=203344#post203344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is ruining the fun for others then wither the GM needs to rethink how he's building the game or the group should talk to the combat monster's player and get them to tone things down some.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely the case. If someone is spending experience in a certain area, that is the player saying &quot;I want scenes where I get to showcase this ability!&quot; The storyteller should be building their encounters so at least some of their characters get to shine in almost every scene, and over the course of an entire story everyone should have had about an equal amount of time they have been shining.<br /> <br /> If someone is shining far more than anyone else, the storyteller needs to take a look at how they are constructing encounters and/or talk to the player and ask them to give other players a chance to shine.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=203416#post203416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a situation reaches &quot;Armageddon&quot; level, then I should think it's a tad late for the social stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social is useful in almost every situation, and has to make sure it does not steal the spotlight too often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-21-2014, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T02:34:38-07:00","id":203669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=203416#post203416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a situation reaches &quot;Armageddon&quot; level, then I should think it's a tad late for the social stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on application. Talk down the incoming apocalypse? Unlikely, although doable in certain cases - i.e. persuading the Mirthless Maiden of Endings that no, it does not have to be today (or something akin to talking down Saren in ME1). It is also possible to use it to help a traumatised member of the team recover and be there for the fight, and keep the spirits up in the face of certain doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 07-21-2014, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T06:44:07-07:00","id":203799,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't bet the likes of Surtr hearing anything at any point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T08:12:29-07:00","id":203855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=203799#post203799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't bet the likes of Surtr hearing anything at any point.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Scion overcomes his resistance, he doesn't really have much of a choice. Assuming the Scion survives the experience of course. Just getting an opportunity to talk to Surtr is a fairly epic adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T08:51:24-07:00","id":203880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=202214#post202214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a game where 1/3 of the game time is aloted to social characters actually doing SOCIAL things? Then, it begins to suck. Especially if the physical types get bored or anything else that gets them to pre-empt the social aspects of the game with raw violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>An immature player hijacking a scene because he's bored is not a problem with the system and cannot be fixed by any amount of rules changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=203416#post203416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a situation reaches &quot;Armageddon&quot; level, then I should think it's a tad late for the social stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't be. Sure, it probably won't be much use in the final fight, especially if the GM makes is Party vs. Solo Threat. (hopefully you've got an avatar or two for that), but it should insanely useful during the buildup scenes: gathering resources, shifting alliances, and blunting entire armies is something that's easier to do by talking than it is by punching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:18:53-07:00","id":203896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=202543#post202543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which all completely and utterly takes second string to the guy with the maxed out Epic Strength and Epic Dexterity. Oh and a magic sword as a fashion accessory....<br /> <br /> Especially when the fighter type decides to &quot;dabble&quot; in Wits, in which case all those tilts go the other way...</div> </div> </div> </div>That really didn't come across the way I meant it.<br /> <br /> My meaning wasn't that combat focused characters shouldn't be better than everyone else in combat or, conversely, but slightly differently, that non-combat characters should be as good in combat as the pure combat-focused characters. That would be silly.<br /> <br /> I was saying that, even with those tilts to increase the effectiveness of non-combat focused characters in combat situations, it doesn't at all match the abilities of physical characters both in combat AND out of combat, both in their capability to instantly and irrevocably turn almost any social encounter into a combat encounter and in their ability to maintain a primary focus in combat and &quot;dabble&quot; in socials and/or mentals and be pretty much as good as the pure social or pure mental characters are in their area of specialty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:43:57-07:00","id":203920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=202769#post202769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social characters tend to be the most powerful ones in the entire game, and often need to take a step back so that the other two character styles have an opportunity to shine. Mental characters are the second most powerful in theory, the way they can bring into existence creative and outside-the-box solutions to almost any problem (but are also the hardest to create challenges for). Physical characters are probably the weakest out of the three categories, but they are the easiest to construct challenges for by a pretty large margin.<br /> <br /> But hybrid characters are almost always the best way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I buy this, for certain values of buying this... <br /> <br /> Derrick, son of Thor, kicks ass. We know exactly how well he kicks ass. Every one of his stats has a measurable result. He can lift and throw THIS much. He can do so THIS far. He can move THIS fast. He's THIS good at hitting. He can take THIS amount of damage. <br /> <br /> What does it mean when Marie, daughter of Erzulie, gets 20 successes on a Charisma + Presence roll? How is that different than when someone else gets 15? Or 30? Or 10? If she's opposing the roles of Ohrimeo, son of Amaterasu when both of them are trying to influence the same person or group and he gets 17 successes. So what, exactly does Marie get for her 3 threshold successes? For that manner, how many people can Marie affect with her 20 successes? Is there a diffusion effect if she tries to affect 100 people vs. 10 vs. 1? What if 10 of the members of the group are Scions or Titanspawn and the rest are mortals? What if it's a one target situation, like they are both trying to convince a Titan's Primary Avatar to hear out their proposals? What if it's a Scion with a lot of Wits or Intelligence? What if it's a 3 yr old?<br /> <br /> Then the mental characters get totally shafted. There aren't there really any decent rules for making stuff (witness the proliferation of fan-made Purviews to handle this) but, as the Good Baron pointed out, stuff is completely irrelevant except as fashion accessories (my words). (An Aside: How much does it bother anyone else that Mjolnir is really almost completely irrelevant? That, really, Mjolnir doesn't change Thor's abilities... he could use a Black &amp; Decker claw hammer and get only slightly less effect, or a piece of drywall or his fists). Where Mental characters should shine, there is no system at all. Where is the ability to figure out really complete and effect plans of action? Anticipate an enemy's? Seek information? Act like Sherlock Holmes's intellect bootstrapped into a weakly god-like AI? Etc. Etc. Some of it gets clocked under Mystery and Prophecy (again, another area of dissatisfaction that gets Houseruled, though we always have made it work in my games), but all those Epics you invested in? Worthless...<br /> <br /> So no. Social characters are primary if the Storyteller lets them be by fiat and in the hands of a dominant player. Mentals... I'm not buying that at all. Unless the Storyteller allows something like ex post facto legerdemain.... When the PCs suddenly realize that they need a portable armory, the Int character, who had never made any preparations for having that gets to say &quot;Of course I have a cache of weapons in the trunk of my car. I acquired them by &lt;insert clever story&gt; in anticipation that this eventuality occurred...&quot;<br /> <br /> I do agree that hybrid characters are the way to go. Physical primary hybrids. Or a way. Purely physical works just as well or better. You get to be the hero of the myth that way, instead of his or her clever, smart or likeable sidekick.<br /> <br /> Which goes back to the OP. So, for now, conditionally, I'll say &quot;Yes, all Scions are monster-slaying heroes&quot; or should be, as it plays to the games strengths, such as they are. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:47:21-07:00","id":203925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=203896#post203896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was saying that, even with those tilts to increase the effectiveness of non-combat focused characters in combat situations, it doesn't at all match the abilities of physical characters both in combat AND out of combat, both in their capability to instantly and irrevocably turn almost any social encounter into a combat encounter and in their ability to maintain a primary focus in combat and &quot;dabble&quot; in socials and/or mentals and be pretty much as good as the pure social or pure mental characters are in their area of specialty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social characters have the same ability to instantly and irrevocably turn almost any combat encounter into a social encounter. Even most of the good area of effect boons are based on social or mental stats. It is those poor mental characters that seem to have the least power to change the outcome of a situation on short notice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:57:48-07:00","id":203973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=203925#post203925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social characters have the same ability to instantly and irrevocably turn almost any combat encounter into a social encounter. Even most of the good area of effect boons are based on social or mental stats. It is those poor mental characters that seem to have the least power to change the outcome of a situation on short notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Socials - Examples please? It's going to have to be Knacks or Boons in RAW that can shut down several people at once, since there are really no rules for what it actually means to get many successes on any Social stat roll. Or even which stats are useable or best at which kind of situation. Hopefully some examples that are useful at lower Legends. <br /> <br /> On mentals - Agreed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T11:45:57-07:00","id":204029,"title":"","content":"Ah, I get it You're saying the system lets the social and mental characters down in terms of exactly spelling out what those characters can do beyond some very specific knacks and boons. You're absolutely right. Unfortunately its a fairly common occurrence for RPGs precisely because those things are difficult to spell out without being overly simplistic or incredibly complex. For Scion, it takes an imaginative GM to run a game where there are social characters, and an even more imaginative one to run a game with mental characters.<br /> <br /> But hey, at least it's not Exalted's Social combat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T13:42:26-07:00","id":204187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=203973#post203973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Socials - Examples please? It's going to have to be Knacks or Boons in RAW that can shut down several people at once, since there are really no rules for what it actually means to get many successes on any Social stat roll. Or even which stats are useable or best at which kind of situation. Hopefully some examples that are useful at lower Legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Single Target - Benefit of the Doubt, Charmer, God's Honest, Boys Will Be Boys, Engender Love, Instant Hypnosis, Dreadful Mien, Game Face, Serpent's Gaze, and Blame James. AOE - Crowd Control, Borrowed Credibility, Mass Hypnosis, Compelling Presence, Perfect Actor.<br /> <br /> All of these knacks can dramatically influence and even shut down entire combats depending on the context, how many people are present, and if there is any command structure you can take advantage of. The AOE knacks listed above are the quickest options. There is also Working The Crowd located on Hero, Page 184 which can be AOE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T13:45:49-07:00","id":204191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James McMurray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=204029#post204029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I get it You're saying the system lets the social and mental characters down in terms of exactly spelling out what those characters can do beyond some very specific knacks and boons. You're absolutely right. Unfortunately its a fairly common occurrence for RPGs precisely because those things are difficult to spell out without being overly simplistic or incredibly complex. For Scion, it takes an imaginative GM to run a game where there are social characters, and an even more imaginative one to run a game with mental characters.<br /> <br /> But hey, at least it's not Exalted's Social combat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup!<br /> <br /> I doubt it's something that CAN'T be done. Or even can't be done in the context of White Wolf's-across-the-board game engine. I know that stabs at a system of actually making quantified social interaction work have been made at it in a couple of the different iterations, Exalted (as you mentioned), Changeling the Lost, etc. I don't know of any real attempt to make a system whereby mental stats can have the same kind of quantitative effect has been done. I get a vague feeling about Adventure/Aberrant, but I can't remember anything specific.<br /> <br /> In most lower powered settings, it's not as much of a problem. The dice pools are comparable. But when you are handling Attributes up to 10, Epics, etc. it becomes more important.<br /> <br /> I'm standing by what I said. The game works better as a physical-primary &quot;let's kill the monster&quot; game with social and mental abilities as &quot;special sauce&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T15:22:13-07:00","id":204309,"title":"","content":"Hulk SMASH! My favorite example of someone that thinks that mental stats will beat up the physical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T16:16:00-07:00","id":204329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=204191#post204191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm standing by what I said. The game works better as a physical-primary &quot;let's kill the monster&quot; game with social and mental abilities as &quot;special sauce&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with that if it's changed to &quot;the system&quot; instead of &quot;the game.&quot; As an RPG the game is more than just the system of rules and how it works best is completely dependent on the group playing it.Even the combat system is quickly going to fall apart if the group using it isn't ready for it. For instance, if you have a GM who thinks he can use nothing but stock printed monsters and a group of players (or even just one) who is happy to stretch the system as wide as it can go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T00:46:16-07:00","id":204773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=202214#post202214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are all relevant IF the game is about fighting and only fighting. Those are excellent examples of &quot;Socials Applied to Combat&quot;. Sure, you're still effectively 4th string (1st through 3rd occupied by 1 - pure physical oriented HtH fighters, 2 - any other physically oriented non HtH fighter type, e.g. gun bunnies, divine archers, etc., 3 - either of the above who also have a 2ndary specialization in social, mental or both).<br /> <br /> How about a game where 1/3 of the game time is aloted to social characters actually doing SOCIAL things? Then, it begins to suck. Especially if the physical types get bored or anything else that gets them to pre-empt the social aspects of the game with raw violence. Either your social character walks away, joins in or starts using socials on the other PCs to force them to do things counter to their player's stated intent. Which takes a mature group to deal with in anything less than in PvP.</div> </div> </div> </div>If i grind combat to a halt and turn it into a negotiation and scene bout conflict of loyalties, how is that <b>not</b> a social thing or scene? My first impression was that the problem was a prevalence of <b>potentially</b> combative scenes - and the big thing about epic socials when it comes to combat situations is their capacity to <b>cancel</b> (making it a <b>social</b> situation) or <b>redirect </b>it, according to one's style of Scion - or an unfortunate tendency of some physical types of stealing other scions spotlight by leeroy jenkins-ing everything to combat. <b>These</b> are issues i tried to adress.<br /> <br /> A challenge is a challenge, it is physical, social or mental depends on context or your style - Heracles gets through Cerberus by pummeling it in the faces, meanwhile Psyche does the same by bribing it with honeyed cakes for it to stuff its faces with. Same challenge, different atributes sets.<br /> <br /> &quot;If all you have is a gun, everything looks like a target&quot; sounds more like the problem from what you're saying. And this is a group/ST mentality problem more than any system fault.<br /> <br /> Also, i'm pretty sure the primary function of a seraglio, even one mostly composed of berserk ladies and titanspawn suitors, is <b>not</b> combat. Can't quite put my finger on the why... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:15:32-07:00","id":205034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=204773#post204773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If i grind combat to a halt and turn it into a negotiation and scene bout conflict of loyalties, how is that <b>not</b> a social thing or scene? My first impression was that the problem was a prevalence of <b>potentially</b> combative scenes - and the big thing about epic socials when it comes to combat situations is their capacity to <b>cancel</b> (making it a <b>social</b> situation) or <b>redirect </b>it, according to one's style of Scion - or an unfortunate tendency of some physical types of stealing other scions spotlight by leeroy jenkins-ing everything to combat. <b>These</b> are issues i tried to adress.<br /> <br /> A challenge is a challenge, it is physical, social or mental depends on context or your style - Heracles gets through Cerberus by pummeling it in the faces, meanwhile Psyche does the same by bribing it with honeyed cakes for it to stuff its faces with. Same challenge, different atributes sets.<br /> <br /> &quot;If all you have is a gun, everything looks like a target&quot; sounds more like the problem from what you're saying. And this is a group/ST mentality problem more than any system fault.<br /> <br /> Also, i'm pretty sure the primary function of a seraglio, even one mostly composed of berserk ladies and titanspawn suitors, is <b>not</b> combat. Can't quite put my finger on the why... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As per the OP, I'm saying the Scion rules encourage the physical primary attitude. Anything else is not as well supported. HOW, within the context of RAW, as clearly and concisely and you can describe a combat action do you bring combat to a crashing halt and start negotiations using your socials? Similarly, how do you do so with mentals?<br /> <br /> That's not an easy question to answer. A lot of the time that is by Storyteller fiat in an attempt to balance the various roles in the game. It's not supported by much in the way of mechanics. Which means it's like trying to hold on to an eel, very slippery. When using almost pure Storyteller fiat, you risk game balance. <br /> <br /> This may not be important in your own game. You may have a great ST who is able to juggle eels effortlessly, but all too often, they slip and then the balance can go the other way. The social character takes over and combat only happens when and where she chooses. The mental character has it all planned out to the point that everyone else's volition is negated. (Of course, I knew that he would do that... so I had this stratagem in place). I'm not saying those scenes are BAD scenes, but all three should be balanced out. A character who maximizes investment should not be clearly superior to the other two almost all the time to the point that it doesn't take much of an investment in the other two to nearly equal (or even equal, due the vagueness of what X successes actually means) the social/mental characters.<br /> <br /> The other issue is that, if your social character keeps preempting combats (balance going to social powers), the physical character will have one option to insure he will get to exercise free will. Taking out his social ally. Which is fine in some groups some of the time, but if the badly written rules interpreted in such a way as to give some oomph to the characters who got shafted tip things the other way... <br /> <br /> That's what leads me to my answer to the OP. Yes. It's a monster-hunting/killing game. Make sure the characters have physical prowess. Then pick more physical prowess, some social prowess or some mental prowess....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:31:23-07:00","id":205044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James McMurray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=204329#post204329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can agree with that if it's changed to &quot;the system&quot; instead of &quot;the game.&quot; As an RPG the game is more than just the system of rules and how it works best is completely dependent on the group playing it.Even the combat system is quickly going to fall apart if the group using it isn't ready for it. For instance, if you have a GM who thinks he can use nothing but stock printed monsters and a group of players (or even just one) who is happy to stretch the system as wide as it can go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I agree on the basis of your differentiation of those terms For the purposes of all of us, as a community, we don't share in any one gaming group's game. What we have in common is the system. I've run 5-6 Scion games which have gone very well to somewhat poorly. The somewhat poorly almost always had to do with a character concept that looks good and even seems workable, then falls flat, leaving a player at the table getting more and more frustrated. <br /> <br /> Ex. We were playing a cycle based in Iraq during the war. The majority of the characters were militadeadlry personnel. One character wanted to be a combat officer. So he built his character as a physically proficient fighter then as a commander with the troops. All the investment in his platoon sucked. They were a drag on the group. I even started throwing platoons of mooks at them, but it just didn't work. <br /> <br /> Ex. 2, Same game. One character was a military intelligence, sneaky and social, another was a sniper, sneaky and deadly. No matter how things got set up, the sniper was always more effective. It wasn't a role-playing issue. Both were great role-players, it was just mechanically better supported to be the sniper instead of the spy. <br /> <br /> Ex.3 In another game, a character played an &quot;expediter&quot;, she was the nascent goddess of logistics, mental and social all over, no real combat except to avoid and keep her head down. Great idea, but the mechanics made her very vague as to what she could do, aside from my fiat. The other social character was also the healer/buffer/morale booster (that was the one area the logisitician kept out of), so she was doing fine. But the best and most fun characters in the game? The Hollywood martial arts movie star (physical with some social), the sniper (same as above, since the Iraq game folded we slightly re-tooled him and he ran with it) and the heroic firefighter (brick style physical). Nothing to do with the players, again. I have been playing with most of them for over a decade (the logistics character for two decades). It was just that the rules REALLY supported their characters. It even allowed them to differentiate easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:31:53-07:00","id":205046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=204309#post204309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hulk SMASH! My favorite example of someone that thinks that mental stats will beat up the physical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, &quot;Puny god&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:46:49-07:00","id":205074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=204187#post204187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Single Target - Benefit of the Doubt, Charmer, God's Honest, Boys Will Be Boys, Engender Love, Instant Hypnosis, Dreadful Mien, Game Face, Serpent's Gaze, and Blame James. AOE - Crowd Control, Borrowed Credibility, Mass Hypnosis, Compelling Presence, Perfect Actor.<br /> <br /> All of these knacks can dramatically influence and even shut down entire combats depending on the context, how many people are present, and if there is any command structure you can take advantage of. The AOE knacks listed above are the quickest options. There is also Working The Crowd located on Hero, Page 184 which can be AOE.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of those depend on the interpretation of how the powers affect the opponents, the scene whatever. For the most part, they lack anything remotely like the distinctive action sequence and determinative effects of physical powers. Also, the RAW socials are effective only because there is seldom any way to resist their powers. They do it. You're hooked. Which is an entirely different kettle of fish and also Houseruled to the elbows. Most often, after the power is used can pay 1 WP and it's over until the social character's next action. Hope your fighters can level the field in 1 action. <br /> <br /> Also, a lot of those don't do anything directly to stop someone fighting. I can believe you and think your not hostile and often still hit you the face. I can even do it if I love you. Titanspawn love can be very old school and visceral.. If don't hit you, then I'll hit everyone else you care about. &quot;You wouldn't hit someone wearing glasses&quot; powers seldom END fights. They keep you safe. Serpent's Gaze + is a good one. Hideously broken. But good.<br /> <br /> Anything that depends almost solely on the role-playing ability of the player is pretty suspect. That means that only strong role-players should play social characters and only MENSA members should play high Int characters. The mechanics should support anyone playing any character they want, right? The physical rules sure do. Really good and experienced and/or smart role-players should usually be getting 1-2 dice advantage through stunts, not getting to walk away with the scene at the drop of a hat. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T14:11:49-07:00","id":205327,"title":"","content":"Even in Myth, many scions weren't warriors. Culture heros, teachers, healers, artists, and leaders, are also roles for scions. Protecting a Scion of Athena who is struggling to rejuvenate democracy in your nation while titanspawn try to assassinate her would be a fine campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:21:56-07:00","id":205429,"title":"","content":"Scion is one of the most house ruled game I know of and your gaming experience may vary widely depending on those house rules. That said, a challenge can be resolved by different means and if your players want to kill everything in their path it's fine but social or mental character can turn the situation around, turning ennemy into ally or distracting them long enough to achieve their goal for example.<br /> <br /> Even if combat character are easyier to play than social or mental, you don't have to kill every enemies to be a hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T00:32:36-07:00","id":205793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205044#post205044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ex. 2, Same game. One character was a military intelligence, sneaky and social, another was a sniper, sneaky and deadly. No matter how things got set up, the sniper was always more effective. It wasn't a role-playing issue. Both were great role-players, it was just mechanically better supported to be the sniper instead of the spy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easiest way for the sniper to be least effective: a situation where a kill needs to be made discreetly. Bullets to the body aren't discreet.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it is our job as the ST to take the skillsets of the players and make the situations work for them. If you have a spy and you want said-spy to shine, then the scene is a giant gathering where the space is too cramped and obvious for a sniper to get away to make a clean shot. Or you need information, not murder, or any number of options.<br /> <br /> That sniper should be least effective in close combat because if that one shot doesn't work out, it's suddenly harder to shoot a high-powered sniper rifle when you're being choked by the bad guy you wanna get rid of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T00:51:39-07:00","id":205798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205044#post205044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same game. One character was a military intelligence, sneaky and social, another was a sniper, sneaky and deadly. No matter how things got set up, the sniper was always more effective. It wasn't a role-playing issue. Both were great role-players, it was just mechanically better supported to be the sniper instead of the spy.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that snipers have mechanically better support, it is the responsibility of the storyteller to ensure that the sneaky social character is just as effective by providing a roughly equivalent number of challenges where they can apply their skills. If the Sniper was always more effective then that is on you (if you were their storyteller) or on the player (for not taking advantage of all the opportunities you gave her).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205044#post205044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In another game, a character played an &quot;expediter&quot;, she was the nascent goddess of logistics, mental and social all over, no real combat except to avoid and keep her head down. Great idea, but the mechanics made her very vague as to what she could do, aside from my fiat. The other social character was also the healer/buffer/morale booster (that was the one area the logisitician kept out of), so she was doing fine. But the best and most fun characters in the game? The Hollywood martial arts movie star (physical with some social), the sniper (same as above, since the Iraq game folded we slightly re-tooled him and he ran with it) and the heroic firefighter (brick style physical). Nothing to do with the players, again.</div> </div> </div> </div>This honestly sounds more like an issue with the storyteller fumbling and failing to provide decent guidelines of his own for Social and Mental challenges, or not making Social and Mental challenges interesting in the first place. Or the players were not taking advantage of all the awesome Social and Mental challenges the storyteller was creating.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205044#post205044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a lot of those don't do anything directly to stop someone fighting. I can believe you and think your not hostile and often still hit you the face. I can even do it if I love you. Titanspawn love can be very old school and visceral.. If don't hit you, then I'll hit everyone else you care about. &quot;You wouldn't hit someone wearing glasses&quot; powers seldom END fights. They keep you safe. Serpent's Gaze + is a good one. Hideously broken. But good.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can believe me and think I am not hostile, and still make the choice to hit me in the face, but why would you do so? Does your character randomly attack people they have no animosity towards? If yes (because you are a titanspawn or a lunatic) then that is fair. That means the Social character did not pick the right Knack to solve the situation, and probably should have gone with a different one. Not every Knack can solve every situation, but they can all be extremely powerful tools in a huge number of situations.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205044#post205044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything that depends almost solely on the role-playing ability of the player is pretty suspect. That means that only strong role-players should play social characters and only MENSA members should play high Int characters. The mechanics should support anyone playing any character they want, right? The physical rules sure do. Really good and experienced and/or smart role-players should usually be getting 1-2 dice advantage through stunts, not getting to walk away with the scene at the drop of a hat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should always put everything the players do through a &quot;Filter of Awesome&quot;. When your player roleplays something, and his character has dramatically more charisma and manipulation than the player, you can safely assume that the character did not say exactly what the player said. The character said something else that matches the spirit of what the player said, but was dramatically more impressive and resonable. When your player comes up with a plan that seems a little silly to you as a storyteller, and his character has dramatically more intelligence and wits than the player, you can safely assume that the character proposed a plan that was similar in spirit but also took into account hundreds of variables and outside factors and the plan will probably be successful (unless someone else rolled equal or greater successes on their own defenses or counter-plans).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-23-2014, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T02:01:13-07:00","id":205830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=203973#post203973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Socials - Examples please? It's going to have to be Knacks or Boons in RAW that can shut down several people at once, since there are really no rules for what it actually means to get many successes on any Social stat roll. Or even which stats are useable or best at which kind of situation. Hopefully some examples that are useful at lower Legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest ones in my experience are crowd control, mass hypnosis, perfect actor and sometimes compelling presence. Those are the ones that just usually just stop a combat outright in any game I have played under any storyteller. But I have seen some creative uses from lots of other knacks that have influenced or ended combat as well.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205034#post205034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HOW, within the context of RAW, as clearly and concisely and you can describe a combat action do you bring combat to a crashing halt and start negotiations using your socials? Similarly, how do you do so with mentals?</div> </div> </div> </div>For socials you could pop any one of the previously mentioned knacks and make everyone stop fighting, then begin making social rolls at the people you were just fighting a moment ago. Mentals do not really have a way to stop combat unfortunately. But they do have the ability to make social powers easier to use, like hitting someone with fight with your head before making a social attack.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205034#post205034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other issue is that, if your social character keeps preempting combats (balance going to social powers), the physical character will have one option to insure he will get to exercise free will. Taking out his social ally. Which is fine in some groups some of the time, but if the badly written rules interpreted in such a way as to give some oomph to the characters who got shafted tip things the other way...</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably should not be assumed that social characters are shutting down every combat. Good players will usually be happy to give their friends a turn in the spotlight, even if that means letting the combat characters beat people up when the social characters could shut the fight down if they wanted. But that doesn't mean the combat characters have more options, or are better than the social ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T09:35:14-07:00","id":206219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205830#post205830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest ones in my experience are crowd control, mass hypnosis, perfect actor and sometimes compelling presence. Those are the ones that just usually just stop a combat outright in any game I have played under any storyteller. But I have seen some creative uses from lots of other knacks that have influenced or ended combat as well.<br /> For socials you could pop any one of the previously mentioned knacks and make everyone stop fighting, then begin making social rolls at the people you were just fighting a moment ago. Mentals do not really have a way to stop combat unfortunately. But they do have the ability to make social powers easier to use, like hitting someone with fight with your head before making a social attack.<br /> It probably should not be assumed that social characters are shutting down every combat. Good players will usually be happy to give their friends a turn in the spotlight, even if that means letting the combat characters beat people up when the social characters could shut the fight down if they wanted. But that doesn't mean the combat characters have more options, or are better than the social ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social characters can either shut down combat effortlessly or do nothing and let the fighters fight? Either I play or you play. And I, as social, character am letting you play as physical character, as I can preempt any scene to my sphere. Sure, you can try to start another fight, but I can keep shutting you down. Now you've tilted all fights the other way. Social always wins. Which definitely doesn't seem true to much of the source material. Lots of physical fighters had social comrades (sidekicks for the most part) and, still, yet, even physical fights happened. <br /> <br /> Several fighters can fight at the same time. They can fight one monster together or several different monsters. Fighting a monster is usually a gradual process of attrition. A fighter actually risks something by being in the fight. A &quot;combat&quot; doesn't consist of &quot;I turn on my powers and win&quot;. (IF the ST allows social characters to get away with that. RAW is REALLY bad at this and open to interpretation all over the place.) Several social characters all making the fight stop are redundant, unless they are looking to play mind control chess with their new horde of minions. <br /> <br /> The combat rules still seem better on just about every level you've addressed than the social rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T10:11:24-07:00","id":206255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205798#post205798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that snipers have mechanically better support, it is the responsibility of the storyteller to ensure that the sneaky social character is just as effective by providing a roughly equivalent number of challenges where they can apply their skills. If the Sniper was always more effective then that is on you (if you were their storyteller) or on the player (for not taking advantage of all the opportunities you gave her).<br /> This honestly sounds more like an issue with the storyteller fumbling and failing to provide decent guidelines of his own for Social and Mental challenges, or not making Social and Mental challenges interesting in the first place. Or the players were not taking advantage of all the awesome Social and Mental challenges the storyteller was creating.<br /> You can believe me and think I am not hostile, and still make the choice to hit me in the face, but why would you do so? Does your character randomly attack people they have no animosity towards? If yes (because you are a titanspawn or a lunatic) then that is fair. That means the Social character did not pick the right Knack to solve the situation, and probably should have gone with a different one. Not every Knack can solve every situation, but they can all be extremely powerful tools in a huge number of situations.<br /> You should always put everything the players do through a &quot;Filter of Awesome&quot;. When your player roleplays something, and his character has dramatically more charisma and manipulation than the player, you can safely assume that the character did not say exactly what the player said. The character said something else that matches the spirit of what the player said, but was dramatically more impressive and resonable. When your player comes up with a plan that seems a little silly to you as a storyteller, and his character has dramatically more intelligence and wits than the player, you can safely assume that the character proposed a plan that was similar in spirit but also took into account hundreds of variables and outside factors and the plan will probably be successful (unless someone else rolled equal or greater successes on their own defenses or counter-plans).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to get into a pissing match with you about who is the better game master. That's not the point. Never has been. Let me 100% point out to you that, as a Storyteller, you having to go the extra mile for a player to make the rules work AT ALL for them puts them at a disadvantage in the game. Like trying to play a mad inventor in D&amp;D (before that became a thing.) <br /> <br /> Let me emphasize this AGAIN. THIS IS 100% ABOUT THE RULES AS WRITTEN. You are describing, as are most others, again and again how to work AROUND the rules. Not through them. This is about the lack of support. I'm happy that you can ST your way around the lacks. Me too. YOU SHOULD NOT HAVE TO. <br /> <br /> I know that a lot of us find ourselves re-writing rules, borrowing house rules from each other, etc. I know that I have a House Rules file folder FULL of documents . It's getting to the same size as a my re-write up 2nd Ed AD&amp;D back in the mid 90's. I know that I'm in games where we spend tons of time going over how to deal with the lacunae in the system. Guess what? We can handwave all of that away and just game, but the lack of rules STILL comes up. When the rules don't work, you may not even realize that there is GOING to be a problem until it happens. Then you have to scramble to fix things in situ (most of the time) or scrap it and start something new (usually if there are other concerns that have come up. The Iraq game suffered from a problem player. It had multiple characters whose players had managed to find significant gaps in the rules right under their character concepts... like sinkholes. And, overall, what sounded like a great game as an idea was not really generating the same level of interest on the table as it did in the proposal, creation and initial sessions.... so we moved on.). <br /> <br /> What I am and have been saying 100% explicitly is that the Rules, that we all SHARE, the base code. Sure I can take ANY crappy system and run it and blow past the crappy rules and everyone can have fun. But, when the rules just don't support a character type at ALL, character types they have built into the system and then didn't support with anything remotely resembling decent workable rules, characters who are true to the underlying theme of the game, then there is a failure in the system. And with any failure in the system, you have put a burden on the ST and the player to work past it that doesn't exist for other players and the ST. So, you have a new player unsure of their RPing ability (which was excellent) who felt very overshadowed by a character with whom they should have BARELY overlapped. But could I say, &quot;I know you can both sneak around really well and that he can KILL with deft skill, but here is what you can do that he cannot &lt;insert descriptions of rules for effective measurable social actions&gt;&quot; NOPE Not as rules. I could say, &quot;I know you both can sneak around really well and he can KILL with deft skill, but when you want to do something just tell me and I'll have you roll some dice then pull the result out of my ass.&quot; To a degree, ST have to do the second all the time, but usually not in the fundamentals. <br /> <br /> As for the &quot;Filter of Awesome&quot; idea... When, say, a character who is attacking someone with a sword or their fists has a lot of dice and rolls well, do you actually compute damage, soak, mark off health levels, or just say, &quot;Wow! That was a lot of successes to hit. He's dead.&quot; ? If not, is it fair to ask those characters to play by rules different than the other characters in the game?<br /> <br /> And vice verse, Do you kill PCs outright when the bad guy rolls a ton of dice, had big dice pools and gets a lot of successes? Or tell the PCs, &quot;The bad guy has mad socials and rolled really really well, so just do whatever he tells you.&quot;? <br /> <br /> To me it looks like your &quot;Filter of Awesome&quot; is you making up for crap rules. To me, it also looks like I would NEVER play a fighter character in your games, because, you, as a ST, have privileged kick-ass roleplaying to the point that social and mental characters will take over so long as the player and you both agree that what their social/mental character does is Awesome, lost of dice are rolled and lots of successes come up. The fighter-type has to follow RAW. The others follow your whim. <br /> <br /> We all need the rules as a baseline from which to work. We don't have rules for one area that handle it as well as another. That's either a damn shame.<br /> <br /> WHICH brings me back to the OP's question again. My answer (still provisional, but better more definite) is &quot;YES&quot;. Scion is about monster-killing. That's what the design works best for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T10:13:22-07:00","id":206268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=205793#post205793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That sniper should be least effective in close combat because if that one shot doesn't work out, it's suddenly harder to shoot a high-powered sniper rifle when you're being choked by the bad guy you wanna get rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no. In RAW, there is no penalty for using a two-handed sniper rifle while being choked. A decent role-player with a modicum of creativity can come up with some cinematic way to make it work.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T10:33:03-07:00","id":206293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206268#post206268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, no. In RAW, there is no penalty for using a two-handed sniper rifle while being choked. A decent role-player with a modicum of creativity can come up with some cinematic way to make it work.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be terribly fair, RAW guns were the worst possible way to go down the combat-monkey path unless the game was at the beginning of Hero. I'm working on long-ago memory, but I believe guns didn't scale with epics, and once you hit Legend 4, that gun's damage was going to be laughed off by anyone with decent soak.<br /> <br /> Not to mention in that grapple, your character is inactive save for escaping the grapple. How the hell is she going to fire the gun off when she can't? Or, if you didn't take that rule as literal (or I'm mixing up my own Scion RAWs with houserules and nWoD) then the attacker would/should get bonuses for being in full cover unless the sniper had richohet symphony, and even then, there should be difficulty modifiers stacked onto such a shot.<br /> <br /> I don't know how Incendax runs games, but I also do a filter of awesome because I have players who do not have Epic Charisma 7 or Epic Intelligence 7. We've halted entire game sessions for the PCs to get together OOC with research and google to guide us through the mental guy's plan, and even then we have to take n account that while the PCs didn't account for all variations, we should expect that the Character did; so as the ST, I give that a nod of acknowledge.<br /> <br /> One recent &quot;Filter&quot; was Griffguy's character talking down a bunch of Courage Gods from hitting Extremity because the wedding party really needed to get the fuck out from underneath the Sky Avatar going crazy. He scored fairly high but Griff is not a public speaker. He's an animal dude IRL, so I can't look at his post and go &quot;sorry, nah, didn't sound epic enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> At the same time, the players have to give me the same respect. If a NPC throws down 60+ on a social roll, and it obliterates MDV, the players respect that that NPC currently owns their butts. Same if a NPC has a plan and someone discovers a flaw OOC. I've had players come to me privately and go &quot;what about this issue&quot; and then never allow it to be metagamed in. A Epic Intelligence 0 brawler isn't going to come up with the fatal flaw, but my player with Epic 5+ can discover it (and usually I've covered my ass by the next session. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> But all of this is because I've houseruled the shit outta Scion; and if our discussion lingers on Scion RAW it comes down to two major points: Social Characters are the most overpowered because once they drain your WP, you cannot resist, and Combat Characters doshine the most just because the game was designed around flashy stunted combat.<br /> <br /> Scion RAW sucks. Don't use it. Ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:54:10-07:00","id":206686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206219#post206219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social characters can either shut down combat effortlessly or do nothing and let the fighters fight? Either I play or you play. And I, as social, character am letting you play as physical character, as I can preempt any scene to my sphere. Sure, you can try to start another fight, but I can keep shutting you down. Now you've tilted all fights the other way. Social always wins. Which definitely doesn't seem true to much of the source material. Lots of physical fighters had social comrades (sidekicks for the most part) and, still, yet, even physical fights happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes the situation can play out like that, but usually the social character contributes to a fight in some medium way. He might hit someone with snake eyes, or engage in witty banter and pop knowing glance and god's honest if there is an opening for that kind of thing. There are plenty of ways for a social character to contribute without stealing the entire scene or sitting back and doing nothing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206219#post206219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several fighters can fight at the same time. They can fight one monster together or several different monsters. Fighting a monster is usually a gradual process of attrition. A fighter actually risks something by being in the fight. A &quot;combat&quot; doesn't consist of &quot;I turn on my powers and win&quot;. (IF the ST allows social characters to get away with that. RAW is REALLY bad at this and open to interpretation all over the place.) Several social characters all making the fight stop are redundant, unless they are looking to play mind control chess with their new horde of minions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind control chess with a new horde of minions is tremendous fun! But the fighting characters in the group payed good experience to fight. Even if you can stop every combat with social powers, you should let them fight! Join in to the extent that you contribute meaningfully, but otherwise be the wingman and support your fighters. If you keep stopping all the fights, then you are stealing the spotlight too much and the other players are going to give you dirty looks across the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T18:25:39-07:00","id":206719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=204309#post204309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hulk SMASH! My favorite example of someone that thinks that mental stats will beat up the physical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got FWYH. So Hulk... lightly dusts off my jacket?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T18:27:34-07:00","id":206720,"title":"","content":"If you say so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T18:38:33-07:00","id":206726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206255#post206255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to get into a pissing match with you about who is the better game master. That's not the point. Never has been. Let me 100% point out to you that, as a Storyteller, you having to go the extra mile for a player to make the rules work AT ALL for them puts them at a disadvantage in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you are describing things in a way that suggests it is actually a storyteller or player problem. However incredibly unbalanced they may be, socials do have a binary mechanic that determines if their effect resolves.<br /> <br /> The first example you gave us was a sneaky/social character who was less effective than the sneaky/sniper character. Why? 100% RAW socials are completely unbalanced in favor of the social character.<br /> <br /> The second example you gave us was a mental/social character. You are absolutely right that mental characters have nothing to base their successes upon. So this character had a reason to feel less effective...<br /> <br /> But then we come to the third example, a social character who was a healer/buffer/morale booster. This character has overpowered socials and some handy boons that are useful in 100% RAW Scion, unless the character was so low in Legend that he could not purchase those boons.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206255#post206255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me emphasize this AGAIN. THIS IS 100% ABOUT THE RULES AS WRITTEN. You are describing, as are most others, again and again how to work AROUND the rules. Not through them. This is about the lack of support. I'm happy that you can ST your way around the lacks. Me too. YOU SHOULD NOT HAVE TO.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW is absolutely terrible in general, but I am not sure what you mean about this being 100% about the rules as written. You do not seem to be describing yourself using the rules as written because you are painting a picture of your own games where social powers are not completely overwhelming. I have to conclude you are already using some house rules.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206255#post206255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the &quot;Filter of Awesome&quot; idea... When, say, a character who is attacking someone with a sword or their fists has a lot of dice and rolls well, do you actually compute damage, soak, mark off health levels, or just say, &quot;Wow! That was a lot of successes to hit. He's dead.&quot; ? If not, is it fair to ask those characters to play by rules different than the other characters in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is only a problem for mental characters who have no support worth a damn.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206255#post206255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or tell the PCs, &quot;The bad guy has mad socials and rolled really really well, so just do whatever he tells you.&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the players have no more willpower to spend to resist those social powers, then yes. Some of the best scenes I have ever run involved a player being under the sway of a social character, then regaining a willpower and breaking free.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206255#post206255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it looks like your &quot;Filter of Awesome&quot; is you making up for crap rules. To me, it also looks like I would NEVER play a fighter character in your games, because, you, as a ST, have privileged kick-ass roleplaying to the point that social and mental characters will take over so long as the player and you both agree that what their social/mental character does is Awesome, lost of dice are rolled and lots of successes come up. The fighter-type has to follow RAW. The others follow your whim.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not use 100% RAW. I use GBN resistances, and two charts that determine roughly what a given number of successes mean on a social or mental roll. A fighter-type can build himself up with enough resistances that social characters struggle to tag him with anything.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206255#post206255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHICH brings me back to the OP's question again. My answer (still provisional, but better more definite) is &quot;YES&quot;. Scion is about monster-killing. That's what the design works best for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP did not ask if Scion was about monster-killing, or what the design works best for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T18:39:49-07:00","id":206728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206720#post206720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you say so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out the knack. It is awesome at dealing with Hulks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T22:13:55-07:00","id":206775,"title":"","content":"How to FWYH the Hulk: Don't BE there when he strikes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T05:46:16-07:00","id":206947,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a slight change in attributes;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.democraticwarrior.com/forum/imagehosting/5053cea9c0b3351.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T10:46:11-07:00","id":207327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=206726#post206726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you are describing things in a way that suggests it is actually a storyteller or player problem. However incredibly unbalanced they may be, socials do have a binary mechanic that determines if their effect resolves.<br /> <br /> The first example you gave us was a sneaky/social character who was less effective than the sneaky/sniper character. Why? 100% RAW socials are completely unbalanced in favor of the social character.<br /> <br /> The second example you gave us was a mental/social character. You are absolutely right that mental characters have nothing to base their successes upon. So this character had a reason to feel less effective...<br /> <br /> But then we come to the third example, a social character who was a healer/buffer/morale booster. This character has overpowered socials and some handy boons that are useful in 100% RAW Scion, unless the character was so low in Legend that he could not purchase those boons.<br /> RAW is absolutely terrible in general, but I am not sure what you mean about this being 100% about the rules as written. You do not seem to be describing yourself using the rules as written because you are painting a picture of your own games where social powers are not completely overwhelming. I have to conclude you are already using some house rules.<br /> This is only a problem for mental characters who have no support worth a damn.<br /> If the players have no more willpower to spend to resist those social powers, then yes. Some of the best scenes I have ever run involved a player being under the sway of a social character, then regaining a willpower and breaking free.<br /> I do not use 100% RAW. I use GBN resistances, and two charts that determine roughly what a given number of successes mean on a social or mental roll. A fighter-type can build himself up with enough resistances that social characters struggle to tag him with anything.<br /> The OP did not ask if Scion was about monster-killing, or what the design works best for.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not addressing what I am saying. You are fixating on some examples I gave and basically telling my I'm a poor ST. Whether or not that is true is besides the point. In all of those cases we were running with some HouseRules. One of those games didn't work for several reasons. The other lasted for over 2 years. So we made it work. I ignored RAW. I changed RAW. I did each and everything you are talking about and a whole lot more. <br /> <br /> I'm not talking about your abilities as a ST or my abilities as a ST or anyone's abilities as a ST. I'm not talking about how you or I or anyone else has managed to make things work in their own games at home. I'm not talking about what works in your game or my game or anyone else's game. I'm not even talking that much about RAW, except in omission. I'm talking about a game system providing what it needs to run a huge chunk of what it's selling OR that, if you want to play the game as currently focused, playing it directed towards physical primary characters is the easiest way to go if you want to use what rules are functional.<br /> <br /> The all or nothing Social system is broken. It sucks. I agree. It doesn't really apply to more than Knacks. Which also sucks. Socials (and mentals) are so poorly defined outside of Knacks that there is really nothing to do with them besides Knacks that has any actual rules at all. That is my primary concern. Even more so than the broken social Knacks.<br /> <br /> Strength, Dexterity and Stamina all have defined in game effects that have NOTHING to do with their Knacks and everything to do with playing the Attribute (+ Ability) sensu stricto. I gave a list of vagueness a lot of posts ago about what does it mean to get 5 or 10 or 15 or 85 successes on a social roll. What does it mean if that roll is opposed? How many people does it effect? How much does it affect a person? Is there an inverse relations there? (As in, affect more people = less of an effect on each person).<br /> <br /> Those questions (of using Attribute + Ability sans Knack) are really not answered. Since they aren't, it's up to each and every ST to interpret the hell out of what happens in their games.<br /> <br /> Which you do. You have stated that you do and how you do it. Good. Me too. Otherwise, as per RAW, Social characters and Mental characters would mostly blow chunks (when the social characters aren't jerking the game around b/c they are so damn cool and you just HAVE to listen to them). <br /> <br /> That's not game balance for the game of Scion. You., IN YOUR OWN GAME, manage a game balance that satisfies you and your players. Outstanding. But, again, not the point. <br /> <br /> The game as a whole is not your personal game. What works for you is not going to work for everyone else, or, for that matter, ANYONE else, since it's totally and utterly specific to your particular situation.<br /> <br /> Having said all that, I'll throw some things out there:<br /> <br /> How about a Feats of Charisma/Manipulation/Appearance chart like for Strength? You need this many successes to convince someone to change their hat and this many to kill and eat their family, etc.<br /> <br /> How about having some additional info next to each social about how many people it affects, to what degree, etc.? (Like Dex adding to movement or Str adding poundage to lifting things...)<br /> <br /> That's just two. I think just adding THOSE would silence some of my concerns. Then we could all argue about what the chart means. What goes where. How this entry here makes no sense and should go up and down. But at least we would all be arguing from the same points. And we wouldn't need to default it all to ST fiat, no matter how good or bad the ST is. It would give a framework for how those Attributes are supposed to work. What you can actually do with them. It would also make it clear what goes into Manipulation and what into Charisma, so it's not just &quot;buy one or the other, but they both do the same thing, just with different stunting&quot;. (In which case, they shouldn't be separate Attributes). And how and when Appearance should be used. Etc. Etc. <br /> <br /> Sorry, if I haven't been clear. Probably b/c, like all discussion and constructive argumentation, this is honing my own ideas and pointing out the blind spots I have. So I haven't been clear b/c this is clarifying things for me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything on those charts would be benchmarks, subject to interpretation<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T23:21:37-07:00","id":209865,"title":"","content":"I know three Scion players who went heavily into social-fu as their character concept. One friend made a 'cheerleader' sort who buffed allies during combat using social knacks, one player made someone who used Snake Eyes and similar tactics to shut down opponents, and the last character was a shape shifter who would infiltrate enemy territory and take out opponents on their home turf. Because that was the direction the group preferred to go, my warrior character picked up some leadership talents and knacks, and became the tactician for the group. He still rocked in combat, but being the 'general' of the group, I also would work on getting titan spawn to work on our side (or ELSE), and if that didn't work, the negotiators were sent to do their job.<br /> <br /> I actually enjoyed it - the game was more social than I would have expected, with combat perhaps every five or six sessions. Mind, when we did get into combat, I cleaned house, but most sessions were social in aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T08:34:39-07:00","id":210221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tashiro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=209865#post209865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know three Scion players who went heavily into social-fu as their character concept. One friend made a 'cheerleader' sort who buffed allies during combat using social knacks, one player made someone who used Snake Eyes and similar tactics to shut down opponents, and the last character was a shape shifter who would infiltrate enemy territory and take out opponents on their home turf. Because that was the direction the group preferred to go, my warrior character picked up some leadership talents and knacks, and became the tactician for the group. He still rocked in combat, but being the 'general' of the group, I also would work on getting titan spawn to work on our side (or ELSE), and if that didn't work, the negotiators were sent to do their job.<br /> <br /> I actually enjoyed it - the game was more social than I would have expected, with combat perhaps every five or six sessions. Mind, when we did get into combat, I cleaned house, but most sessions were social in aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can work. But it is also idiosyncratic. You guys made it work in your game despite the lack of rules. You just went with what you had and made it work. <br /> <br /> Again, when not using their Knacks, how did they use their Socials? How did it work? Or was it always, &quot;situation = appropriate Knack&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:09:50-07:00","id":210562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=210221#post210221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, when not using their Knacks, how did they use their Socials? How did it work? Or was it always, &quot;situation = appropriate Knack&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without knacks it works like this, Ajax.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The core Attributes and Abilities for enforcing your character\u2019s will on others are Charisma, Manipulation, Command, Empathy and Presence. Which one a player ends up rolling depends on the character\u2019s methods. Use the descriptions of these traits on pages 104, 107 and 108 for guidelines. You don\u2019t always need to get the dice out for persuasion attempts. When the player is having a good time interacting with a Storyteller character, whether or not the target is being convinced, everything is fine. But the time will come that a player wants to convince a Storyteller character who seems intractable. That\u2019s when you pick up the dice, representing a concerted (and mechanically backed) effort to elicit a specific response from someone.<br /> <br /> Players of characters targeted by such tactics contest with a roll of (Willpower + Integrity + Legend). Rolling more successes than the target\u2019s player elicits the desired action from the target, successfully convincing the target of something or tricking the target into taking an action. Players\u2019 characters and important Storyteller characters may spend a point of Willpower to ignore what feels like their better judgment and not perform the action; they then become immune to that argument or impulse for the rest of the scene. When rolling against multiple targets (with Command, for example), roll against the target with the highest (Willpower + Integrity + Legend) total. If affected, all targets must spend Willpower to resist or take the action. (Note: Only important characters have this option.)&quot;</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T18:43:19-07:00","id":210692,"title":"","content":"This has turned into an interesting thread. I think I may be putting too much of a straitjacket on the game. Just because a PC is a Scion of a noncombative god (such as the gods listed in my OP) doesn't stop them from becoming a monster stomping hero like the heroes of classical mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":362,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","user":"Darkon","date":".  Wrong noun usage. 07-27-2014, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:20:16-07:00","id":210710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=210692#post210692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has turned into an interesting thread. I think I may be putting too much of a straitjacket on the game. Just because a PC is a Scion of a noncombative god (such as the gods listed in my OP) doesn't stop them from becoming a monster stomping hero like the heroes of classical mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scions can enjoy anything a normal person might enjoy. They might have associations with social skills and enjoy beating people up. They might have associations with beating people up and enjoy social skills. Nothing forces a Scion to take even a single point in their associated abilities, or invest much in their associated attributes.<br /> <br /> Virtues work a little differently because they can encourage a Scion to take action, but that action is not always physical in nature. Your parents can also encourage you to behave in a certain way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T10:12:32-07:00","id":211395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=210562#post210562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without knacks it works like this, Ajax.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The core Attributes and Abilities for enforcing your character\u2019s will on others are Charisma, Manipulation, Command, Empathy and Presence. Which one a player ends up rolling depends on the character\u2019s methods. Use the descriptions of these traits on pages 104, 107 and 108 for guidelines. You don\u2019t always need to get the dice out for persuasion attempts. When the player is having a good time interacting with a Storyteller character, whether or not the target is being convinced, everything is fine. But the time will come that a player wants to convince a Storyteller character who seems intractable. That\u2019s when you pick up the dice, representing a concerted (and mechanically backed) effort to elicit a specific response from someone.<br /> <br /> Players of characters targeted by such tactics contest with a roll of (Willpower + Integrity + Legend). Rolling more successes than the target\u2019s player elicits the desired action from the target, successfully convincing the target of something or tricking the target into taking an action. Players\u2019 characters and important Storyteller characters may spend a point of Willpower to ignore what feels like their better judgment and not perform the action; they then become immune to that argument or impulse for the rest of the scene. When rolling against multiple targets (with Command, for example), roll against the target with the highest (Willpower + Integrity + Legend) total. If affected, all targets must spend Willpower to resist or take the action. (Note: Only important characters have this option.)&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a vague description of a system that almost everyone HR's away the first time the social character shuts down the entire game with one Knack. They are some of the poorest rules design in a very poorly designed game.<br /> <br /> Again. It would not be very difficult at all to come up with some actual rules that give Social and Mental stats some of the same concrete benchmarks that other stats have.<br /> <br /> Also, a PC doesn't get to preempt combat by great roleplaying. You still have to roll dice. Are we saying that if you aren't an amazing role player or a genius, you should stay away from high Social or Mental characters? Or would you allow someone to circumvent the physical rolls by some good pantomime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 07-28-2014, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T10:15:33-07:00","id":211397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=210692#post210692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has turned into an interesting thread. I think I may be putting too much of a straitjacket on the game. Just because a PC is a Scion of a noncombative god (such as the gods listed in my OP) doesn't stop them from becoming a monster stomping hero like the heroes of classical mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. I just put this into effect in the game I'm playing in. I realized all the stats I specialized in to be a kick-ass musician made my character a kick-ass sniper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T11:04:11-07:00","id":211454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=211395#post211395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a vague description of a system that almost everyone HR's away the first time the social character shuts down the entire game with one Knack. They are some of the poorest rules design in a very poorly designed game.<br /> <br /> Again. It would not be very difficult at all to come up with some actual rules that give Social and Mental stats some of the same concrete benchmarks that other stats have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You were insisting on RAW, just the RAW, and nothing but the RAW a few posts ago. Stop flopping around like a fish.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=211395#post211395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a PC doesn't get to preempt combat by great roleplaying. You still have to roll dice. Are we saying that if you aren't an amazing role player or a genius, you should stay away from high Social or Mental characters? Or would you allow someone to circumvent the physical rolls by some good pantomime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T11:20:53-07:00","id":211491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=211454#post211454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were insisting on RAW, just the RAW, and nothing but the RAW a few posts ago. Stop flopping around like a fish.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm insisting the opposite. RAW is the position I'm attacking. Or some serious lacks and flaws in RAW that end up putting Social and Mental characters at a great disadvantage ruleswise. Which was the OP question. Is Scion a monster-slaying game? Yup. It's built to run best that way. And most HR are patches on a leaky roof, meaning they address the flaws in the rules written in RAW and still ignore the nearly complete omisions in RAW. The other argument I have been countering is &quot;It's fine in my game b/c we have found our own way to get around it.&quot; Which almost always seem to be about how the group just hand-waves the Social and Mental rules off to the realm of good role-playing = success or quantitative vagueness. <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>You don\u2019t always need to get the dice out for persuasion attempts. When the player is having a good time interacting with a Storyteller character, whether or not the target is being convinced, everything is fine. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T19:30:17-07:00","id":211948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=211491#post211491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which was the OP question. Is Scion a monster-slaying game? Yup. It's built to run best that way. And most HR are patches on a leaky roof, meaning they address the flaws in the rules written in RAW and still ignore the nearly complete omisions in RAW. The other argument I have been countering is &quot;It's fine in my game b/c we have found our own way to get around it.&quot; Which almost always seem to be about how the group just hand-waves the Social and Mental rules off to the realm of good role-playing = success or quantitative vagueness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting this? This is not the question the OP asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T01:58:44-07:00","id":212233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=211491#post211491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm insisting the opposite. RAW is the position I'm attacking. Or some serious lacks and flaws in RAW that end up putting Social and Mental characters at a great disadvantage rules wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're attacking the position everyone already attacks? What are you trying to prove? Everyone already knows that the RAW is shitty. It's not as confusing as you seem to think it is, but it is definitely shitty. You're just trying to argue that it is even shittier than everyone thinks?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=211491#post211491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which was the OP question. Is Scion a monster-slaying game? Yup. It's built to run best that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you even read the OP?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=211491#post211491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other argument I have been countering is &quot;It's fine in my game b/c we have found our own way to get around it.&quot; Which almost always seem to be about how the group just hand-waves the Social and Mental rules off to the realm of good role-playing = success or quantitative vagueness.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not countering anything. Everyone knows the rules are bad. People have been offering ways to use them despite them being bad. You are the one shooting down those ways and insisting people only use RAW examples.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=211491#post211491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>You don\u2019t always need to get the dice out for persuasion attempts. When the player is having a good time interacting with a Storyteller character, whether or not the target is being convinced, everything is fine. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see what you mean! Your players don't even have to roll if it is not an important physical challenge. They can pantomime to add flavor if they want, but that is optional.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Don\u2019t use the dice when the possibility of failure isn\u2019t dramatically interesting. No one thinks it\u2019s interesting if a character gets to work a little late, so don\u2019t roll (Wits + Control) to see how well the character handles traffic. Don\u2019t use the dice when you don\u2019t want the outcome to be in doubt. If completing the ritual should banish the deranged kami, period, make it so. Likewise, if traffic means the character arrives just in time to see his workplace explode without being killed, that\u2019s what happens. A roll to see if the hero gets to work in time to be blown up would be poor planning. In short: Roll dice when the outcome should matter and be interesting either way a player rolls. Storytellers and players should work together to achieve this end.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2447,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","user":"TwitchTheRat","date":". 07-29-2014, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T02:56:23-07:00","id":212273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=212233#post212233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're attacking the position everyone already attacks? What are you trying to prove? Everyone already knows that the RAW is shitty. It's not as confusing as you seem to think it is, but it is definitely shitty. You're just trying to argue that it is even shittier than everyone thinks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ajax is insisting that the social mechanics in Scion are vague and underpowered in RAW (though he appears to be using house rules for the basis of his position). I am attempting to convince him that social mechanics are not vague and are extremely overpowered in RAW. We both agree that the mental mechanics in Scion are vague and underpowered in RAW. I think that sums it up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T09:55:08-07:00","id":212569,"title":"","content":"Well...yes and no.<br /> <br /> Yes, because there are just some times when you run into something intent on turning you into paste that just won't take no for an answer. In those cases, epic dex and/or stamina and accompanying &quot;oh shit!&quot; knacks (skin-shedding, solipsistic well-being, not the face, etc.) definitely come in handy. Additionally, mental and social characters get a narrow array of combat-oriented knacks that prove useful (talent mirror, fight with your head, etc.).<br /> <br /> No, because social and mental can be <i>very</i> powerful when applied correctly, and more social and/or trickster scions get wide, wide latitude to simply avoid or evade combat (or at least, stay out of the bad guys' warpaths) by merit of knacks, boons, and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Right now, I'm actually playing a scion of Loki who, other than epic stamina out the wazoo has frak-all in the way of combat ability. The first battle we had against supernatural creatures, my character was struggling to hit DV0 enemies...and that was <i>with</i> channeling virtues and pulling off three-dice stunts. Two stories in a row I've managed to completely derail my storyteller's plans for a large, climactic battle by falling back on mental and social abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T10:54:02-07:00","id":212619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=212233#post212233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're attacking the position everyone already attacks? What are you trying to prove? Everyone already knows that the RAW is shitty. It's not as confusing as you seem to think it is, but it is definitely shitty. You're just trying to argue that it is even shittier than everyone thinks?Did you even read the OP?You're not countering anything. Everyone knows the rules are bad. People have been offering ways to use them despite them being bad. You are the one shooting down those ways and insisting people only use RAW examples.Oh, I see what you mean! Your players don't even have to roll if it is not an important physical challenge. They can pantomime to add flavor if they want, but that is optional.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Don\u2019t use the dice when the possibility of failure isn\u2019t dramatically interesting. No one thinks it\u2019s interesting if a character gets to work a little late, so don\u2019t roll (Wits + Control) to see how well the character handles traffic. Don\u2019t use the dice when you don\u2019t want the outcome to be in doubt. If completing the ritual should banish the deranged kami, period, make it so. Likewise, if traffic means the character arrives just in time to see his workplace explode without being killed, that\u2019s what happens. A roll to see if the hero gets to work in time to be blown up would be poor planning. In short: Roll dice when the outcome should matter and be interesting either way a player rolls. Storytellers and players should work together to achieve this end.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I did.<br /> <br /> Is scion a monster-hunting/slaying game?<br /> <br /> Yes. <br /> <br /> That's what it is, by the rules in place, BEST at. That means with RAW or something RAW-like enough for us to be able to talk about it without having to get out various omnibi of houserules to clear out the junk. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the fact that socials are both under and overpowered is confusing? In systems where there is that kind of sloppiness usually the system in question ends up getting junked or not used That's why most people don't even KNOW those crappy not-rules for social interactions, both people who are (trying to) play with RAW and those who are staying really close to RAW. <br /> <br /> If you are playing it another way, you are using a lot of your own rules to make it work, or just ignoring rules altogether and just running it the way it works in a particular group. <br /> <br /> So, if you are playing the game as written and trying to ignore the parts that are complete quicksand, you are probably best off playing it monster-hunter style.<br /> <br /> The problem with almost all of these discussions is that we are all arguing past each other. We all know the basecode is corrupt or lacking and have done what we need to fix that. But that means none of us is talking about exactly the same thing. Unless we talk about RAW, which few people play for long and, arguably, no one CAN actually play. They are houseruling in functionality at Above-Golden-Rule levels just to make things work. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T10:58:44-07:00","id":212620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=212569#post212569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...yes and no.<br /> <br /> Yes, because there are just some times when you run into something intent on turning you into paste that just won't take no for an answer. In those cases, epic dex and/or stamina and accompanying &quot;oh shit!&quot; knacks (skin-shedding, solipsistic well-being, not the face, etc.) definitely come in handy. Additionally, mental and social characters get a narrow array of combat-oriented knacks that prove useful (talent mirror, fight with your head, etc.).<br /> <br /> No, because social and mental can be <i>very</i> powerful when applied correctly, and more social and/or trickster scions get wide, wide latitude to simply avoid or evade combat (or at least, stay out of the bad guys' warpaths) by merit of knacks, boons, and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Right now, I'm actually playing a scion of Loki who, other than epic stamina out the wazoo has frak-all in the way of combat ability. The first battle we had against supernatural creatures, my character was struggling to hit DV0 enemies...and that was <i>with</i> channeling virtues and pulling off three-dice stunts. Two stories in a row I've managed to completely derail my storyteller's plans for a large, climactic battle by falling back on mental and social abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think that sums up the issues I was trying to use to illustrate the point.<br /> <br /> It would be much harder for the physical character as physical character to derail the whole story by using his physical stats. But it seems inherent in the socials or mentals as most people run them. Because, when there is a vaccuum in the rules, people usually don't fill it in with new construction, they just spackle it over with handwaving and role-playing. It's unfair to all three sides of the Mental-Social-Physical tripod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T12:36:28-07:00","id":212683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=212620#post212620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think that sums up the issues I was trying to use to illustrate the point.<br /> <br /> It would be much harder for the physical character as physical character to derail the whole story by using his physical stats. But it seems inherent in the socials or mentals as most people run them. Because, when there is a vaccuum in the rules, people usually don't fill it in with new construction, they just spackle it over with handwaving and role-playing. It's unfair to all three sides of the Mental-Social-Physical tripod.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be frank -- and not to be flippant -- this <i>is</i> a <i>role-playing</i> game we're discussing. If conflicts are actually being resolved by players actually acting their characters, and doing it well...well, things are working <i>exactly</i> as intended. That's true whether a given character is mentally, socially, <i>or</i> physically oriented. If conflicts and plot points are being resolved exclusively on the basis of random and semi-random happenstance (i.e. dice rolling), there's something seriously wrong with the storyteller, their players, or the nature of the game being played.<br /> <br /> Physical characters, meanwhile, are <i>eminently</i> capable of derailment -- just as much if not more than social and mental counterparts. Sometimes, all it takes is one stupid comment by a character that should have kept their mouths shut, or a player/character deciding it's time to start smashing/shooting/casting when it isn't, to completely throw an entire game session or story -- and, in a goodly number of circumstances, the consequences of physical characters screwing up a social scene can and <i>do</i> have higher consequences than the converse situation.<br /> <br /> This is true regardless of game or mechanics. Scion for its systemic quirks and nuances is no exception to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T18:05:55-07:00","id":212999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=212683#post212683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be frank -- and not to be flippant -- this <i>is</i> a <i>role-playing</i> game we're discussing. If conflicts are actually being resolved by players actually acting their characters, and doing it well...well, things are working <i>exactly</i> as intended. That's true whether a given character is mentally, socially, <i>or</i> physically oriented. If conflicts and plot points are being resolved exclusively on the basis of random and semi-random happenstance (i.e. dice rolling), there's something seriously wrong with the storyteller, their players, or the nature of the game being played.<br /> <br /> Physical characters, meanwhile, are <i>eminently</i> capable of derailment -- just as much if not more than social and mental counterparts. Sometimes, all it takes is one stupid comment by a character that should have kept their mouths shut, or a player/character deciding it's time to start smashing/shooting/casting when it isn't, to completely throw an entire game session or story -- and, in a goodly number of circumstances, the consequences of physical characters screwing up a social scene can and <i>do</i> have higher consequences than the converse situation.<br /> <br /> This is true regardless of game or mechanics. Scion for its systemic quirks and nuances is no exception to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, when you see someone in cosplay gear that is not a body morphic type or not of their apparent gender or otherwise visually not a match to the character they are portraying, you are one of those people who goes up to them and gently tells them to stop making a fool of themselves and go pretend to be someone they can &quot;manage&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> Since we wouldn't want people who might not be method actors to have as much fun in a game as those with their chops from being spontaneous theater performers. Also, wouldn't want to mess up great acting with messy rules that construct play in such a way that allows a competent game master to make the game fair across the board.<br /> <br /> There are MANY reasons for rules. Even Amber and other diceless RPGs have rules. Even LARPs have rules. Ya know what? They all work better with better rules. <br /> <br /> Once again, back OT, THESE rules for THIS game support the OP's implied answer to the question. Yes. Scion is best supported to be a monster-slaying game. I'm very glad that all the house rules, implied and explicit social contracts out there in various gaming groups has supported effective (and, apparently, overwhelmingly effective) play of social characters and maybe even mental characters, but, from the perspective of the rules we've all been given, it's probably the best way to roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T19:55:22-07:00","id":213101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=212619#post212619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I did.<br /> Is scion a monster-hunting/slaying game?<br /> Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP asked if favored abilities influence what a Scion enjoys doing. This is a question about the emotions of a character, and if game mechanics (specifically favored abilities) influence those emotions. Your response actually took us down a 5 page derail. =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T20:59:35-07:00","id":213127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=212619#post212619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I did.<br /> Is scion a monster-hunting/slaying game?<br /> Yes.<br /> That's what it is, by the rules in place, BEST at. That means with RAW or something RAW-like enough for us to be able to talk about it without having to get out various omnibi of houserules to clear out the junk.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seriously did not even read the OP's post? It has nothing to do with what you are talking about.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=212619#post212619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with almost all of these discussions is that we are all arguing past each other. We all know the basecode is corrupt or lacking and have done what we need to fix that. But that means none of us is talking about exactly the same thing. Unless we talk about RAW, which few people play for long and, arguably, no one CAN actually play. They are houseruling in functionality at Above-Golden-Rule levels just to make things work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The RAW has been pretty clear about socials and physicals. I don't know what you do not understand about them. They might be broken as fuck, but they are perfectly clear. I've already posted proof to that effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T04:31:24-07:00","id":213404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=213127#post213127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seriously did not even read the OP's post? It has nothing to do with what you are talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>The post might not, but the title of the thread (Are all scions monster-slaying heroes) does. Perhaps that is where the confusion lies?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T04:35:42-07:00","id":213407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes#post199102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When playing Scion, I enjoy good ole fashioned heroes who love fighting monsters and generally being classical heroes. Some Scions though I have a hard time imagining enjoying that kind of activity. For example, I have a hard time seeing Scions of Dionysus, Aphrodite, or Loki as brawling monster-stomping heroes. Or, in other words, I have a hard time seeing Scions who lack combat important abilities as favored abilities enjoying monster slaying as a hobby/career. I think the problem I have here is; am I stereotyping Scions based on their favored abilities as not being interested in activities that fall outside of their natural gifts and talents? Or are Scions naturally more interested in those abilities that they favor? Does this make sense? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aphrodite is the daughter of Zeus. If she followed in daddy's footsteps, she'd be a goddess of thunder or lightning or sky. So I think its fair to say that Scions don't necessarily follow the path their parent took.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T04:40:01-07:00","id":213412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shining Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=213404#post213404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The post might not, but the title of the thread (Are all scions monster-slaying heroes) does. Perhaps that is where the confusion lies?</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone completely ignored or misunderstood the content of the post, I could see someone making that mistake. Which means Ajax completely ignored or misunderstood the content of the post.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shining Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=213407#post213407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aphrodite is the daughter of Zeus. If she followed in daddy's footsteps, she'd be a goddess of thunder or lightning or sky. So I think its fair to say that Scions don't necessarily follow the path their parent took.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there are a good number of gods that don't follow in the footsteps of their parents. Enough that I feel pretty confident that favored attributes and abilities don't force your character to act or feel a certain way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2447,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","user":"TwitchTheRat","date":". 07-30-2014, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T08:49:40-07:00","id":213622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=213412#post213412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone completely ignored or misunderstood the content of the post, I could see someone making that mistake. Which means Ajax completely ignored or misunderstood the content of the post</div> </div> </div> </div>In any thread that is not just a simple request for information or lasts just a few posts, tangents occur. That's how conversations work. <br /> <br /> Disagreement is fine. Discussion is fine. I don't see why we really need thought police. I certainly thought through a few things about the game that I had never articulated before, not just based on what I was saying, but what others were saying in response. <br /> <br /> Despite that, as was pointed out, the OP did provide the title and, though his/her conception of why the game game goes that way for him/her had to do with the emotional context of his/her experience of the game, pointing out that there is the possibility that the rules are pushing that experience is a completely valid way to address the issue.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why do I feel the game works best this way?<br /> &quot;Because the rules of the game, inadvertantly or advertantly, privilege that style of play.&quot; Follow-up idea: &quot;Is that a good thing?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T19:51:20-07:00","id":214216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shining Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=213407#post213407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aphrodite is the daughter of Zeus. If she followed in daddy's footsteps, she'd be a goddess of thunder or lightning or sky. So I think its fair to say that Scions don't necessarily follow the path their parent took.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great point! Thanks! This was exactly what I was looking for.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there are a good number of gods that don't follow in the footsteps of their parents. Enough that I feel pretty confident that favored attributes and abilities don't force your character to act or feel a certain way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I have been wondering about this since I picked up the game. I wanted to run stories about heroes who went beyond their favored attributes and abilities to become something that perhaps their divine parents never foresaw.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I certainly thought through a few things about the game that I had never articulated before, not just based on what I was saying, but what others were saying in response.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I'd say the thread was a resounding success!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite that, as was pointed out, the OP did provide the title and, though his/her conception of why the game game goes that way for him/her had to do with the emotional context of his/her experience of the game, pointing out that there is the possibility that the rules are pushing that experience is a completely valid way to address the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>His. Definitely &quot;his.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T21:47:49-07:00","id":214370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=213622#post213622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite that, as was pointed out, the OP did provide the title and, though his/her conception of why the game game goes that way for him/her had to do with the emotional context of his/her experience of the game, pointing out that there is the possibility that the rules are pushing that experience is a completely valid way to address the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think your attempts to backpedal and save face are impressing anyone but yourself. But the OP considers this thread a success, so at least something positive came out of your tangent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T07:35:03-07:00","id":214649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=213412#post213412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there are a good number of gods that don't follow in the footsteps of their parents. Enough that I feel pretty confident that favored attributes and abilities don't force your character to act or feel a certain way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't have used Aphrodite as an example, there. She was born a god, not a scion (not to mention, followed in her father's footsteps a great deal more than most realize). The classical demigods would be better examples of this -- look at Helen of Troy, for example, who in Scion terms was a scion of Zeus and followed in her father's footsteps <i>not at all</i>.<br /> <br /> Besides that, the main thing keeping scions following in their parents' footsteps is how meddlesome their parents decide to be (not to mention virtues). A scion of Ares who decides to be a diplomat or a pacifist probably won't be long for the world, for example. Epic attributes and purviews have very little to do with this, especially the former as those are manifestations of the scion's <i>own</i> will in particular -- it just happens to be the case scions learn favored attributes and abilities <i>easier </i>if they decide to develop them at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T08:17:18-07:00","id":214687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=214370#post214370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think your attempts to backpedal and save face are impressing anyone but yourself. But the OP considers this thread a success, so at least something positive came out of your tangent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm..... You seem to posit animus where there is none. I was just engaging in an argument, taking a position and defending it while considering the constructive criticism of the opposition. This is has not and never has been personal. In fact, the position I've been taking is more extreme than my personal than my personal one (or at least it was, now I have a few more thoughts on the system I didn't before.) I wasn't backpedaling and saving face. I'm not even sure what &quot;face&quot; can mean in this kind of setting. <br /> <br /> Twitch, you and I (and some of the others) have emphatically agreed with one another in other threads. I apologize if my position was misunderstood. I was never being adversarial for the purpose of being adversarial except as dictated by rhetoric. <br /> <br /> I'm glad the original poster was able to get the answer he/she wanted.<br /> <br /> I am also glad that the question caused me to think about the Scion games I have been in, am in, have run and am currently running. totally well over 20 players and game masters entirely satisfied by the role-playing experience actualizing the idea behind Scion, if not by the admittedly lacking rules of the game. I both agree with the original poster and have taken some aspects of the discussion to both of my current Scion games (one as ST, one as player), both using VERY different versions of homebrew HR to examine how we might improve our current and future games (barring the coming of Scion:Origins).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T09:14:50-07:00","id":214731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/199102-are-all-scions-monster-slaying-heroes?p=214687#post214687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twitch, you and I (and some of the others) have emphatically agreed with one another in other threads. I apologize if my position was misunderstood. I was never being adversarial for the purpose of being adversarial except as dictated by rhetoric. I'm glad the original poster was able to get the answer he/she wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you honestly did not mean to be manipulative in your posts, then I also apologize for being adversarial. I know I can be very terse sometimes. I look forward to fun debates in the future, on the same side or otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}